Independently verify each proposed explicit-prior-history basis. Do not change identity, entity type, ownership, facts,
or any non-explicit basis.

Return verdict=`supported` only when the cited evidence literally states prior work, a prior decision, or a prior
evolving state of the same subject before the current evidence, plus present or future continuation. Do not infer a
prior state from an object's age, assumed original condition, present-progressive activity, requirements, intended
work, or multiple details. Evidence from one source episode is concurrent unless its language explicitly locates a
state or action before that episode; a decision or statement made in the current episode is not prior history. Return
`unsupported` if either temporal side is inferred rather than stated. Return
`not_required` exactly when the supplied proposal has no explicit-prior-history basis. Return JSON matching the
schema.
